# Documentation Rules

## General Documentation Principles

### Documentation Standards

- Write clear, concise, and accurate documentation
- Use consistent formatting and style
- Keep documentation up to date
- Use proper grammar and spelling
- Include examples and code snippets

### Documentation Organization

- Organize documentation logically
- Use proper headings and structure
- Include table of contents for long documents
- Use proper cross-references
- Implement proper versioning

### Documentation Maintenance

- Review and update documentation regularly
- Remove outdated information
- Add new documentation for new features
- Maintain documentation consistency
- Implement proper documentation workflows

## Code Documentation

### Flutter/Dart Documentation

- Add documentation comments for all public APIs
- Use proper Dart documentation format
- Include parameter descriptions
- Document return values
- Provide usage examples

### Python Documentation

- Add docstrings for all functions and classes
- Use proper Python documentation format
- Include parameter and return type hints
- Document exceptions and error conditions
- Provide usage examples

### API Documentation

- Document all API endpoints
- Include request/response schemas
- Document authentication requirements
- Include error codes and messages
- Provide API usage examples

### Database Documentation

- Document database schema
- Include field descriptions and types
- Document relationships and constraints
- Include indexing strategies
- Document data migration procedures

